{
 "id": "l44",
 "label": "44",
 "title": "Colors",
 "summary": "Basic colors (pulá, asúl, diláw, bérde…), dark colors (asúl na asúl), light colors with murá, shades (mapúla-púla, pulahán) and colors named after things (bérdeng mansánas, gintô)",
 "minutes": 30,
 "goals": [
  "Name the basic colors, including black and white",
  "Talk about brown things and brown skin the Tagalog way",
  "Make dark or bright colors by repeating the color word with a ligature",
  "Make light or pale colors with murá",
  "Make shades with ma- (or mang-) and with -an / -han"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Brown: a gap in Tagalog",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Tagalog does not have a word for every English color. For example, it has **no equivalent for brown** or its shades, such as golden brown. In cooking, golden brown is usually expressed with **pulá** (*red*):"
    },
    {
     "type": "examples",
     "items": [
      {
       "tl": "Prituhin mo ang isdâ hanggáng pumulá.",
       "en": "Fry the fish until it turns golden brown.",
       "parts": [
        [
         "Prituhin",
         "fry",
         "pred"
        ],
        [
         "mo",
         "you",
         "pron"
        ],
        [
         "ang",
         "article",
         "marker"
        ],
        [
         "isdâ",
         "fish",
         "noun"
        ],
        [
         "hanggáng",
         "until",
         "other"
        ],
        [
         "pumulá",
         "turns golden brown",
         "pred"
        ]
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Kayumanggí** is used for the color of the **Filipino race and their skin** (sometimes called **morena**, a word of Spanish origin). It is only used for race and skin color, **not for brown things**."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "For a brown thing or object, use a descriptive phrase with **kulay**:"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Tagalog",
      "Meaning"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[kulay kapé|pred]]",
       "coffee-colored"
      ],
      [
       "[[kulay tsokoláte|pred]]",
       "chocolate-colored"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Brown things"
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "brown",
     "title": "Brown"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
