  {
   "title": "Light colors with murá",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Lighter colors (unless they have their own Tagalog name) take the word **murá**, placed either **before or after** the color."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "english",
     "title": "Three meanings of murá",
     "items": [
      "**pale** or **light** (for colors)",
      "an **unripe fruit**",
      "something that is **cheap or not expensive**"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "English",
      "Tagalog"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "pale blue",
       "[[asúl na murá|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "light green",
       "[[muráng bérde|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "pale yellow",
       "[[diláw na murá|pred]]"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Light colors"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Before or after",
     "t": "After the color, use **na**: asúl **na** murá. Before the color, murá takes **-ng**: murá**ng** bérde."
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "light",
     "title": "Light colors"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Shades",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "There are two ways to show a **shade** of a primary or secondary color:"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "Two formulas",
     "items": [
      "**ma- + the root repeated**, with a hyphen between: mabérde-bérde.",
      "**root + -an** (or **-han**): pulahán, dilawán.",
      "**Asul** and **itim** take **mang-** instead of ma-. In mangasúl-ngasúl, the **ng** of mang- is repeated in the second half after the hyphen."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Color",
      "ma- / mang- form",
      "-an form"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "blue",
       "[[mangasúl-ngasúl|pred]]",
       "[[asúlan|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "green",
       "[[mabérde-bérde|pred]]",
       "[[luntían|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "red",
       "[[mapúla-púla|pred]] / [[mamúla-múla|pred]]",
       "[[pulahán|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "white",
       "[[maputî-putî|pred]] / [[mamutî-mutî|pred]]",
       "[[putián|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "yellow",
       "[[maniláw-niláw|pred]]",
       "[[dilawán|pred]]"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Shades of color"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "remember",
     "title": "Sound changes",
     "t": "After a prefix such as ma-, the first **d** of diláw changes to **n** (maniláw-niláw), and the **p** of pula and puti can change to **m** (mamúla-múla, mamutî-mutî). These changes were covered in earlier lessons."
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "shade",
     "title": "Shades"
    }
   ]
  },
